  "notes": "Warm paper-beige palette (#f2ecde page, #fbf8f1 panels with a 1px #ddd4c0 border, 10px radius) under a near-black #201d18 top bar, which makes the dashboard feel like an editorial ledger rather than a SaaS BI tool. Fraunces serif numerals carry the personality. Categories use a consistent muted hue code (slate blue, orange, plum, teal, taupe) across table dots, bars, bubbles and list markers. The selected row gets a dark left rule plus a beige fill, and the matching bubble gets a thick black outline. Insight-first copy: an H1 sentence summarises the finding, the chart labels its 'quick and lucrative' quadrant, the detail panel splits into 'Worth hunting for' (green eyebrow) and 'First to stop buying' (red eyebrow), and losses are shown in red. In the heatmap, cells with fewer than 6 sold items are dashed and pale to flag low sample size. Segmented controls are dark-filled pills in a beige track. No icons beyond arrow glyphs."
